From: apklayer <noreply@apklayer.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer patch: heavy-tier bisection switches and an FP/SIMD sweep (DIAGNOSTIC)

BERBERIS_HEAVY_DENY splits ldst into excl (exclusive, ordered, CAS), atomic (LSE), pair (LDP/STP) and single, and single into
lit, sp (SP base), ld and st. BERBERIS_HEAVY_SKIP=loop,fwd,local,put,fold,dce,flags,vex,lea,nop,merge,cold,fwdblk,place skips
those heavy optimization passes one by one (disable-heavy-opts in BERBERIS_FLAGS skips all; keep glibc-host-thread-id-handoff
in that list). Unset: nothing changes. Test Arm64HeavyDifferentialFuzz.FpSimdFiniteSweep: random FP/SIMD encodings and
4-instruction chains over finite lane values, heavy vs interpreter (run in a child process), grouped by encoding; it finds
the interpreter's fixed-point FCVTZS/FCVTZU wrapping instead of saturating, SCVTF reading register 31 as non-zero, heavy
accepting a few unallocated encodings, and FP16 signalling-NaN differences (not fixed). Module libberberis_arm64.

